{"diagnosis": "Failing signal is TRAP: cpu trap asserted with tohost FAIL 0xdead during 256-word NOP sled where no illegal opcode is expected. Excerpt at picorv32.v:1446 shows decoder_trigger <= mem_do_rinst || mem_done, causing a second decoder firing on mem_done with stale rdata mis-decoded as illegal and breaking fetch alignment/progress (CYCLES=2009) via cpu at picosoc/picosoc.v:146. Removing || mem_done restores single trigger per fetch.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -1446,4 +1446,4 @@
-		decoder_trigger <= mem_do_rinst || mem_done;
+		decoder_trigger <= mem_do_rinst;
 		decoder_trigger_q <= decoder_trigger;
 		decoder_pseudo_trigger <= 0;
 		decoder_pseudo_trigger_q <= decoder_pseudo_trigger;
", "expected": "tohost PASS (no FAIL 0xdead, no TRAP: cpu trap asserted)"}

